{# Persistent frame: unchanged on every page, kept mounted by the router. #}
<header class="masthead">
  <div class="container">
    {% include "partials/nav.njk" %}

    <a class="masthead__brand" href="/">
      <img class="masthead__logo logo--spin" src="/assets/images/logo.png" alt="" />
      <img class="masthead__wordmark" src="/assets/images/wordmark.png" alt="{{ site.name }}" />
    </a>

    {# Slogan, parked for now:
    <p class="masthead__title">
      {{ site.slogan.lead }} <span class="text-accent">{{ site.slogan.accent }}</span>
    </p>
    #}

    <p class="lead lead--strong">
      The platform that lets <strong class="text-agent">AI agents</strong> run your testing lab
    </p>
  </div>

  {# The thesis sits on the page background so the home page alternates from the very top. #}
  <div class="masthead__principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pillars" data-reveal-group>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "stack-2" %}</span>
            <h3 id="test-suite-standardization" class="pillar__title">Test suite standardization</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">Every suite has the
            <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/#component-model">same structure</a>: suites, groups, tests,
            cases, flows and steps in plain Python, with configuration declared as fields. An AI agent writes it
            without an API to learn, and the controller derives the GUI from it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "code" %}</span>
            <h3 id="continuous-test-development" class="pillar__title">Continuous test development</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">The suite is written from the documentation of the system under test and grows with
            it. As the system changes, the AI agent finds the features the suite does not cover yet and
            <a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/#continuous-expansion">adds the missing tests</a>; every fixed
            bug <a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/#bug-coverage">becomes a test</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "hierarchy" %}</span>
            <h3 id="orchestration" class="pillar__title">Orchestration</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">The AI agent picks the machines from the controller's
            <a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/endpoints/">endpoints file</a>, configures the run in code and
            <a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/running/">runs it across the lab</a>. The controller uploads the
            package to every endpoint and collects the logs and results in one place.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "infinity" %}</span>
            <h3 id="continuous-integration" class="pillar__title">Continuous integration</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">The same suite runs from the pipeline: a
            <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/batches/">snapshot</a> exported from the GUI, or a batch the AI
            agent writes on every merge. A run confirmed by hand and a run started by a pipeline are the same run.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
